---
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Features">
  <section class="page-hero container narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">Project features</p>
    <h1>Present the server like a living expansion.</h1>
    <p>
      This page is designed to hold feature highlights, class overviews, custom systems, challenge modes, and long-form
      project messaging without feeling cramped.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container section-block card-grid three-up">
    <article class="info-card">
      <h2>Rebalanced classes</h2>
      <p>Show spec identities, role shifts, and talent experiments with artwork, patch notes, and forum links.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="info-card">
      <h2>Custom bosses and battlegrounds</h2>
      <p>Feature new encounters, screenshots, trailers, and PvP rule changes in a format players can actually browse.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="info-card">
      <h2>Community-driven roadmap</h2>
      <p>Keep a visible path for future patches, player suggestions, and what is being tested next.</p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="container section-block split-section">
    <div>
      <SectionHeading eyebrow="Expandable structure" title="Suggested feature subpages" />
      <div class="card-grid">
        <article class="mini-feature-card">
          <h3>Classes</h3>
          <p>One page per class, plus balance notes and talent links.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="mini-feature-card">
          <h3>PvP</h3>
          <p>Ranked ladders, event weekends, battleground changes, and arena plans.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="mini-feature-card">
          <h3>PvE</h3>
          <p>Dungeons, raids, challenge encounters, loot, and attunements.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="mini-feature-card">
          <h3>Quality of life</h3>
          <p>Client improvements, UI recommendations, launcher patching, and support guides.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="content-panel">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why this page matters</p>
      <p>
        Larger server sites win because they do not hide their depth. When your content is grouped clearly, the project feels bigger,
        healthier, and easier to trust before a player even downloads the client.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
